course: dictionary
lesson: 2922
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Dramatic is one of them. To work out which meaning fits, read the words around it, which are its context. «The rescue at sea was dramatic, with boats and helicopters racing to save the crew.» Racing and rescue are clues, so dramatic means exciting and full of action here.
explain: Dramatic can also mean sudden and large, a big change, as in «a dramatic rise» on a graph. Look at the words next to it. A rise is a change in numbers, so the meaning is about a big, sudden change.
explain: In everyday talk, «Don't be so dramatic!» is an informal phrase. Someone who is dramatic is showing too much emotion, like a person who makes a huge fuss over a small bump. Read the whole sentence and ask: does this make a fuss, or is it a big change? That tells you which meaning to use.
fact: Dramatic has several meanings, and the sentence around it tells you which one is right.
fact: Dramatic means sudden and large, making a big change, as in «a dramatic change».
fact: Dramatic means exciting and full of action, as in «a dramatic rescue».
fact: Being dramatic, in informal talk, means showing too much emotion: «Don't be so dramatic!»
fact: The adverb is dramatically, made by adding -ally to dramatic, as with basic and basically.
exercise: «The rescue at sea was dramatic, with boats and helicopters racing to save the crew.» What does dramatic mean here? | Showing too much feeling | Quiet and calm | *Exciting and full of action | Sudden and small
exercise: Priya cried over a dropped pencil. Her brother says, «Don't be so dramatic!» What does he mean? | She is acting in a play | She is very rich | She has made a big, sudden change | *She is showing too much emotion
exercise: Which word is the adverb form of dramatic? | dramatic | drama | *dramatically | dramas
test: «The number of visitors rose dramatically in one week.» What does dramatically mean here? | In a quiet, careful way | In a tired way | In a sad way | *In a sudden, big way
test: Which sentence uses dramatic to mean exciting? | A dramatic rise in the number of visitors | The dramatic teacher asked us to sit down | *A chase across the rooftops made the final chapter dramatic | Don't be so dramatic, it is only a scratch
exam: Dashes can make writing more dramatic, but if you use too many, they lose their effect. What should a writer do? | *Use dashes sparingly so they keep their power | Use a dash after every single word | Never use any punctuation at all | Use dashes only in maths lessons
